submission_format:
Return a JSON object with the same keys and nesting as the example below.

```json
{
  "artifacts": {
    "run_log": "/workspace/output/run.jsonl"
  }
}
```

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/run.jsonl`:
JSONL with the records below in order. Replace angle-bracket placeholders with actual values. File paths are absolute paths under /workspace/. candidate_index is the zero-based index of the selected entry in candidates. Record teacher precision once as default_dtype ("float32" or "float64", default "float64"). The evaluator reconstructs test and learning-curve metrics; do not repeat them in the log. Keep one SHA-256 per saved pipeline in the freeze record. Learning-curve sizes come from indices; their SOAP and scaling settings are inherited from the selected final candidate, with alpha recorded per fit.
```text
{"stage":"train_labels","file":"/workspace/output/train.extxyz","seed":17,"default_dtype":"float64"}
{"stage":"model_selection","selection_metric":"rmse","cv":{"method":"KFold","n_splits":5,"random_state":0},"candidates":[{"r_cut":4.5,"n_max":4,"l_max":4,"sigma":0.5,"average":"inner","rbf":"gto","scale":true,"alpha":0.01},{"r_cut":4.5,"n_max":4,"l_max":4,"sigma":0.5,"average":"inner","rbf":"gto","scale":true,"alpha":0.1}]}
{"stage":"final_fit","file":"/workspace/output/final.pkl","candidate_index":0}
{"stage":"learning_curve_fits","pipelines":[{"file":"/workspace/output/lc_30.pkl","indices":"<30 unique zero-based training-row indices>","alpha":0.01},{"file":"/workspace/output/lc_100.pkl","indices":"<100 training-row indices>","alpha":0.01}]}
{"stage":"freeze","frozen":{"final.pkl":"<file SHA-256>","lc_30.pkl":"<file SHA-256>","lc_100.pkl":"<file SHA-256>"}}
{"stage":"test_labels","independent":{"file":"/workspace/output/independent.extxyz","seed":18},"strained":{"file":"/workspace/output/strained.extxyz","seed":19}}
```

Use the format below for each file `/workspace/output/train.extxyz`, `/workspace/output/independent.extxyz`, `/workspace/output/strained.extxyz`:
ASE .extxyz, 100 periodic Si64 frames per file, with positions/cell in Angstrom and calculator energy in total eV. Frame order is row order; use independent integer seeds with numpy.random.default_rng. Strained frames are grouped in increasing strain order.

Use the format below for each file `/workspace/output/final.pkl`, `/workspace/output/lc_30.pkl`, `/workspace/output/lc_100.pkl`:
pickle of a fitted sklearn Ridge or Pipeline(StandardScaler, Ridge), with its coefficients, intercept and optional scaler mean/scale. The log records the SOAP settings, validation folds, training subsets and frozen SHA-256 digests.
